        {
          "type": "tool_use",
          "name": "exec",
          "input": "text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/worktree-rapid-meadow-d5ee/docs/research/tool-harness/2026-09-06-file-native-knowledge-writes.md\\n+# File tools for recoverable Knowledge changes\\n+\\n+Recommend ordinary `read`, `write`, and `edit` over authorized resources, plus\\n+shell access to an isolated editing directory and a trusted publication operation.\\n+Knowledge stays Markdown and Git-compatible. The common interface does not make\\n+every resource writable or give every Node a shell.\\n+\\n+Status: noncanonical pitch for reconsidering #212, dated 2026-09-06. High confidence\\n+in the interface and ownership boundaries; moderate confidence in the proposed\\n+first implementation. No runtime implementation or dependency evaluation has been\\n+performed. Issue bodies and comments are design inputs, not settled requirements.\\n+\\n+## Evidence that changes the decision\\n+\\n+| Finding | Current evidence | Consequence |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| F1 | [#212](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/issues/212) has no comments. It specifies one complete Markdown file, one durable effect per Run, recoverable Git publication, and no generic files or shell. | Its recovery requirements remain useful; its tool shape and scope deserve revision. |\\n+| F2 | [VISION](../../../VISION.md) makes current Markdown files authoritative, including uncommitted changes, and keeps episodic state database-native. [ROADMAP](../../../ROADMAP.md) puts #212 before Profile Space. | File tools fit the destination. Reading only committed Git blobs would regress shipped Knowledge behavior. |\\n+| F3 | [#659](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/pull/659) contains a thin CLI, personal Node, shared Knowledge filesystem extraction, and a hosted adapter. [#672](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/pull/672) and [#673](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/pull/673) are replacement extraction layers. | Put resource operations at the Node/runtime boundary, with hosted and personal authorization adapters. Avoid a second implementation in the CLI. These PRs are open, not shipped evidence. |\\n+| F4 | The #659 source advertises `read_file`, `write_file`, and `process_run`; Knowledge reads still use `knowledge_read`. The separate draft [#539](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/pull/539) advertises a different file/shell tool set. | There is no settled universal CLI tool contract to copy verbatim. Reconcile names and range semantics during integration. |\\n+| F5 | [#547](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/issues/547) covers portable Knowledge identity. The current source in research [#581](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/pull/581) separates origin namespace from current governing authority. | Resource identity must survive relocation and authority transfer. A host path, display name, Git remote, or current authority is insufficient. |\\n+| F6 | [#513](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/issues/513) needs exact accepted Profile revisions; [#552](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/issues/552) needs owner-facing content population. | Share the publication service across agent edits and future owner uploads. Profile activation remains a separate control-plane operation. |\\n+\\n+The #547 comment about claim bundles is unimplemented, explicitly unreviewed\\n+input. It raises useful questions about evidence and currentness, but adding a\\n+general epistemic-permission schema to a file manifest would delay this feature.\\n+Carry source addresses and observed revisions; do not make transported prose an\\n+authorization grant.\\n+\\n+## What to take from OMP and the external examples\\n+\\n+OMP routes resource URLs through its existing file-oriented tools. Its\\n+[`InternalResource` and handler contracts](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/1adcef9762b065c0cef15703fd3e78ecaaa52a3b/packages/coding-agent/src/internal-urls/types.ts)\\n+retain content type, canonical URL, directory shape, and immutability. Its\\n+[`router`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/1adcef9762b065c0cef15703fd3e78ecaaa52a3b/packages/coding-agent/src/internal-urls/router.ts)\\n+dispatches to resource-specific implementations. This is the useful reuse:\\n+familiar verbs and navigation, with the backend retaining semantics.\\n+\\n+Shell interoperability is additional work. OMP has explicit\\n+[`bash` URL-resolution code](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/1adcef9762b065c0cef15703fd3e78ecaaa52a3b/packages/coding-agent/src/tools/bash-skill-urls.ts).\\n+An ordinary `grep` process does not understand `kb://` because a read tool does.\\n+Do not promise POSIX interoperability from a URI router alone, or copy OMP's\\n+process-global registry into hosted tenant authorization.\\n+\\n+[Vercel's filesystem-agent example](https://vercel.com/blog/how-to-build-agents-with-filesystems-and-bash)\\n+uses prepared directories and shell commands to explore business documents. It\\n+supports trying this interaction model; it does not establish llame's recovery,\\n+tenant isolation, or retrieval quality. Public enthusiasm is motivation for an\\n+evaluation, not comparative evidence that `grep` replaces semantic recall.\\n+\\n+[`just-bash`](https://github.com/vercel-labs/just-bash/blob/main/packages/just-bash/README.md)\\n+is a concrete candidate to evaluate: it documents shell syntax, text utilities,\\n+`jq`, in-memory files, mount composition, and copy-on-write adapters. Network and\\n+optional language runtimes can remain disabled. It is simulated shell execution,\\n+not arbitrary native binaries. Its documentation identifies beta status and the\\n+absence of VM isolation; its existence does not certify hosted confinement.\\n+\\n+## Alternatives\\n+\\n+| Option | Benefit | Cost | Judgment |\\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n+| O1: bespoke one-file Knowledge mutation tool | Smallest change to today's hosted catalog | Another domain-specific verb; shell mass edits need a second path | Viable release fallback, weaker interface direction |\\n+| O2: native shell directly on canonical KB directories | Immediate ordinary-file workflows | Host authority, non-replayable side effects, concurrent overwrites, hosted isolation work | Useful only under explicit native policy; insufficient for #212's strong guarantees |\\n+| O3: common file tools, isolated editing directory, trusted Git publication | Familiar workflows; one publication path for file edits and shell output | Editing-view lifecycle and publication recovery must be designed | Recommended |\\n+| O4: universal mounted filesystem for Knowledge, Chats, tools, and remote realms | Maximum apparent uniformity | Drivers, caching, revocation, remote consistency, and invented write semantics | Defer; no first-release user job requires this breadth |\\n+\\n+O3 should start with one Knowledge Space and bounded Markdown changes. One\\n+cross-file reorganization can become one change set; no transaction across spaces\\n+or authorities is implied. The one-note proof in #39 remains the release gate.\\n+\\n+## D1: One path-shaped interface, explicit resource capabilities\\n+\\n+Use `read({path, offset?, limit?})`, `write({path, content})`, and\\n+`edit({path, oldText, newText})`. Start with exact, unique text replacement;\\n+ambiguous or missing matches fail. Hashline editing can be evaluated later.\\n+Preserve the existing bounded line-read conventions instead of introducing a\\n+third range convention beside Knowledge and the experimental CLI.\\n+\\n+A schematic portable path is:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+kb://<origin-namespace>/<space-id>/research/topic.md\\n+```\\n+\\n+The resolver maps it through trusted owner access and node-local bindings. The\\n+origin namespace is stable; the current governing authority and physical route\\n+are separate. Introducing this locator requires defining the minimal namespace\\n+bootstrap together with #547. It does not require enrollment or synchronization.\\n+For an initial owner-local adapter, keep the existing space ID binding internally;\\n+do not invent the namespace by hashing a host path or deriving it from a login.\\n+\\n+The model receives available roots and their capabilities from the harness.\\n+Names help discovery; IDs distinguish resources. A locator grants no access.\\n+Authorization is checked at each live read, editing-view admission, and publish.\\n+Unknown schemes or unavailable resources fail explicitly rather than falling\\n+through into local filesystem access.\\n+\\n+Each read result preserves resource identity, line coordinates, provenance,\\n+continuation, and source trust framing. Add a whole-source revision or digest for\\n+mutation preconditions. The harness retains it; ordinary edits should not require\\n+the model to copy long hashes. A write over existing content requires an observed\\n+base; creation requires observed absence. A partial read cannot authorize blind\\n+replacement of unseen content.\\n+\\n+## D2: A real editing view for shell composition\\n+\\n+Normal Knowledge reads remain live. Opening a writable editing view creates a\\n+bounded snapshot of the selected Space or declared subset, including eligible\\n+uncommitted content, and records its base bytes. Label the view as a snapshot;\\n+subsequent tools in that view see their own edits. Never silently substitute it\\n+for a fresh live Knowledge read.\\n+\\n+The model gets a stable logical working directory, for example:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+/knowledge/<space-id>/\\n+/scratch/\\n+```\\n+\\n+These are execution-view paths, not portable source identities. A manifest maps\\n+them to the authorized resource and snapshot. Exclude `.git`, credentials,\\n+runtime configuration, and files outside the admitted set. Do not give the agent\\n+the Git publisher's repository metadata or credentials.\\n+\\n+Example interaction, with illustrative path spelling:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+read({path: \\\"kb://<namespace>/<space>/research/topic.md\\\", offset: 0, limit: 100})\\n+edit({path: \\\"research/topic.md\\\", oldText: \\\"old claim\\\", newText: \\\"sourced correction\\\"})\\n+bash({command: \\\"grep -R -n 'old claim' .\\\", cwd: \\\"/knowledge/<space>\\\"})\\n+publish({message: \\\"Correct the sourced claim\\\"})\\n+```\\n+\\n+The harness binds `edit`, `bash`, and `publish` to the active editing view;\\n+no caller-selected owner or physical root is accepted. View admission can occur\\n+when the agent selects an advertised writable Space; narrate that transition.\\n+The URI read above obtains current source evidence before that snapshot is opened.\\n+\\n+`write` and `edit` report changes saved in the editing view. `publish` reports\\n+accepted canonical changes separately. It can execute immediately within existing\\n+authorization; the extra verb is a durability boundary, not a mandatory human\\n+approval dialog. Do not disguise commit, activation, or permission operations as\\n+writes to special control files merely to reduce the tool count.\\n+\\n+Evaluate just-bash against these workflows before adopting it. Use one private\\n+execution instance per editing view, bounded authorized input, bounded output,\\n+no network, no injected secrets, and a supervised execution process. A process\\n+alone is not filesystem confinement: hosted execution still needs OS-enforced\\n+restrictions or an equivalent validated isolation boundary. If that dependency\\n+is too large, ship the same file tools without shell first, preserving O3's\\n+publication contract. Do not silently switch to native execution.\\n+\\n+The existing personal Node native executor remains independently useful for\\n+explicitly authorized Workspace tasks. It does not become the hosted KB executor.\\n+Android can implement bounded resource reads without advertising shell support.\\n+\\n+## D3: Git publication is the engineering work that remains\\n+\\n+The trusted publisher takes the editing-view diff, validates paths and content,\\n+rechecks current authority and base revisions, and commits only t